.TH AD_TMUX_WATCH 1 "2026-09-01" "ad 2.0" "ad tools"
.SH NAME
ad_tmux_watch \- open ad_watch + vim in a tmux window with vertical split
.SH SYNOPSIS
.B ad_tmux_watch
<oldfile> <newfile> <opfile> [--ad-layer=<name>]... [options]
.SH DESCRIPTION
.B ad_tmux_watch
creates a new tmux window with two panes side by side:
.RS 4
.IP \(bu 2
Left pane:
.B ad_watch
(displays old, new, diff \(em refreshes on save)
.IP \(bu 2
Right pane:
.B vim
with
.I ad_ops_syntax.vim
(edit ops, :w to refresh left pane)
.RE
.PP
If
<opfile>
doesn't exist, it's generated first via
.BR ad_gen_ops (1)
using the specified
.B --ad-layer
options.
.SH OPTIONS
.TP
.BR --help ", " -h
Show help and exit.
.TP
.BI --ad-layer= NAMERe
Pass to
.B ad_gen_ops
(if generating ops). Repeatable.
.TP
.BI --ad-layer-path= DIR
Pass to
.BR ad_gen_ops .
.TP
.B --no-generate
Don't generate ops even if opfile is missing.
.TP
.B --show-delays
Pass to
.B ad_watch
(keep delay ops in the stream).
.TP
.B --show-decorations
Pass to
.B ad_watch
(keep highlight/dim/fold/sign/marker ops).
.SH EXAMPLES
.TP
Basic usage \(em generates ops if /tmp/ops.tsv doesn't exist:
.B ad_tmux_watch old.py new.py /tmp/ops.tsv --ad-layer=ad_layer_reorder
.TP
Use existing ops file:
.B ad_tmux_watch old.py new.py existing_ops.tsv
.TP
With multiple layers:
.B ad_tmux_watch old.py new.py /tmp/ops.tsv \\\\
.br
.B   --ad-layer=ad_layer_reorder --ad-layer=ad_layer_indent_last
.SH REQUIREMENTS
Requires:
.BR tmux (1),
.BR vim (1),
and the ad tools
.RB ( ad_watch ", " ad_gen_ops ).
Must be run inside a tmux session.
.SH SEE ALSO
.BR ad_watch (1),
.BR ad_gen_ops (1),
.BR ad (1)
.PP
.I scripts/vim/ad_ops_syntax.vim
\(em vim syntax highlighting for op files
.PP
.I docs/design/AD_WATCH_REQUIREMENTS.md
\(em full requirements
